        "original_id": "7d62be45-8e7b-5eac-84a4-c750feb4b6ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ivan Rival, Dwight Duffus\n- Organizations: University of Calgary, University of Ottawa, Emory University\n- Places: Ottawa, Ontario, Canada, Sandy Hill, Rideau Canal\n- Products: Order (journal)\n\nFacts:\n- Ivan Rival was born on March 15, 1947, and he was a Canadian mathematician and computer scientist.\n- Ivan Rival was a professor of mathematics at the University of Calgary and a professor of computer science at the University of Ottawa.\n- Order was founded in 1984 by University of Calgary mathematics professor Ivan Rival.\n- The University of Ottawa main campus is located on 42.5 hectares in the residential neighbourhood of Sandy Hill, adjacent to Ottawa's Rideau Canal.\n- As of 2010, Order's editor in chief was Dwight Duffus, the Goodrich C. White Professor of Mathematics & Computer Science at Emory University and a former student of Ivan Rival.\n- Ivan Rival died on January 22, 2002, in Ottawa, Ontario, Canada.",
